4. Uses a disjunctive constraint to prevent any two items from overlapping
5. Minimizes the area of the larger rectangle (total_x × total_y)
6. Outputs the solution in JSON format with the positions of all items and the dimensions of the larger rectangle

The output will show the optimal placement of items and the minimal required dimensions of the containing rectangle.

