```minizinc
% Parameters
int: l = 9;  % odd positive integer
int: m = (l - 1) div 2;

% Variables
array[1..l] of var -1..1: a;
array[1..l] of var -1..1: b;

% Constraints
% Quadratic constraints (PAF constraints)
constraint forall(s in 1..m) (
    sum([a[i] * a[(i + s - 1) mod l + 1] | i in 1..l]) +
    sum([b[i] * b[(i + s - 1) mod l + 1] | i in 1..l]) = -2
);

% Linear constraints
constraint sum(a) = 1;
constraint sum(b) = 1;

% Symmetry breaking (fix first element to break symmetry)
constraint a[1] = 1;
constraint b[1] = 1;

% Output
output [
    "{",
    join(",", [
        "\"" ++ "a" ++ "\": [" ++ join(",", [show(a[i]) | i in 1..l]) ++ "]",
        "\"" ++ "b" ++ "\": [" ++ join(",", [show(b[i]) | i in 1..l]) ++ "]"
    ]),
    "}"
];
```

This model:
1. Defines the parameters l (given as 9) and calculates m = (l-1)/2
2. Creates two arrays of variables a and b, each of length l, with domain {-1, 1}
3. Implements the m quadratic constraints using the periodic autocorrelation function (PAF)
4. Adds the two linear constraints requiring the sums of a and b to be 1
5. Includes symmetry breaking constraints by fixing the first elements of a and b to 1
6. Outputs the solution in JSON format showing the values of a and b arrays

